{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-promoted, transition metal-free, and strong oxidant-free method for the direct C3-carbamoylation of 2H-indazoles. Using 4CzIPN as a photocatalyst, oxamic acids as carbamoyl sources, and Cs2CO3 as a base under O2 atmosphere, the authors achieved site-selective functionalization. The method was applied to late-stage drug modification, peptide N-terminal modification, and the synthesis of a compound with significant antitumor activity against Ramos cells.",
